<title>POLAND: Polish bourse clears Celuloza and Lentex for trade.</title>
<headline>Polish bourse clears Celuloza and Lentex for trade.</headline>
<dateline>WARSAW 1997-04-09</dateline>
<text>
<p>The supervisory board of the Warsaw Stock Exchange approved for trade on the main market of the bourse the shares of paper firm Celuoza Swiecie SA and textile firm  Lentex SA, the bourse said in a statement.</p>
<p>The Wednesday statement said new share issues of main market firms Boryszew SA and Polisa SA were also cleared for trade.</p>
<p>The board also approved for trade on the parallel market the shares of gauge-maker Apator SA and electrical repair firm Zaklady Remontowe Energetyki Warszawa SA (ZREW), as well as the new share issue of Lubawa SA.</p>
<p>The bourse's board upheld its earlier decision to deny jeans maker Elpo SA, presently listed on the third or &quot;free&quot; market, transfer to the parallel market.</p>
<p>It also cleared for operations brokerage  Dom Inwestycyjny Banku Wschodnio-Europejskiego SA.</p>
<p>-- Warsaw Newsroom +48 22 653 9700</p>
